Leaderboard:
# Plasmid reconstruction leaderboard

Tools are ranked only within their own input track and task, never across them. **Binning reconstruction** (tools that group existing contigs into plasmids) is ranked by length-weighted binning F1; **sequence reassembly** (tools that produce plasmid sequences) by isolate-level CPRR; **classification** (tools that label sequence as plasmid or not) by base-level F1. The ranking score averages per-species means when enough independent isolates exist, over reference tiers 1-2 only, using the samples every ranked tool shares.

## classification (ranked by base-level classification F1)

> Base-level F1 measures detection: how much plasmid sequence is recovered or labelled correctly. It says nothing about whether the sequence is grouped into individual plasmids.

> **PROVISIONAL: primary analysis unavailable.** Population: provisional: all samples (no truth-provenance table, so no sample can be shown to meet the reference requirement). This is not the primary result.

| Rank | Tool | Scored | Completed | Failed | Skipped | **Ranking score** | 95% CI | Basis | CPRR | Mean base F1 | Mean precision | Mean base recall | Significant vs runner-up |
|---:|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|:---|---:|---:|---:|---:|:---|
| 1 | tool_a | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | **0.800** | < 5 independent units | pooled; 1 shared sample(s), 1 cluster(s) | not bin-scored | 0.800 | 0.800 | 0.800 | not assessed |


> **Warning:** Database leakage was NOT assessed. Every database-using tool/sample pair is 'unknown' because no database release date has been filled in (config/tool_database_releases.tsv). Tools that score contigs against a plasmid database or a model trained on one may have seen the truth genomes, so their F1 can be inflated relative to new isolates. Treat their ranking as provisional until the dates are filled in and the screen is re-run.

_Length-weighted binning F1: bases placed in the correct (one-to-one matched) bin, over all truth-plasmid bases (recall) and over all bases the bins align to (precision). CPRR = share of truth plasmids reconstructed correctly (matched, covered, uncontaminated, not split, and -- where truth was not polished with the benchmark's own reads -- high identity). A tool that predicts nothing, or whose run failed, on a plasmid-bearing sample scores 0 there; a sample missing for any other reason is removed from every tool's ranking. CIs resample independent clusters (shared BioProject or clonal group) within each species._

